
  riscvsim › demo 1 · Your first instructions
  Watch five instructions move through the five stages.

   1  # Each line is one instruction. Every cycle, each one
   2  # moves one stage to the right: IF, ID, EX, MEM, WB.
   3  addi x1, x0, 6     # x1 = 0 + 6
   4  addi x2, x0, 7     # x2 = 0 + 7
   5  addi x3, x0, 100   # x3 = 100
   6  addi x5, x0, 1     # x5 = 1
   7  add  x4, x1, x2    # x4 = 6 + 7 = 13

  cycle 1
    IF addi x1, x0, 6  ID ·  EX ·  MEM ·  WB ·
    › The first instruction, addi, is fetched from memory.

  cycle 2
    IF addi x2, x0, 7  ID addi x1, x0, 6  EX ·  MEM ·  WB ·
    › addi is decoded and reads its source registers.

  cycle 3
    IF addi x3, x0, 100  ID addi x2, x0, 7  EX addi x1, x0, 6  MEM ·  WB ·
    › addi is computing in the ALU; everything else moves one stage on.

  cycle 4
    IF addi x5, x0, 1  ID addi x3,x0…  EX addi x2,x0,7  MEM addi x1,x0,6  WB ·
    › addi is computing in the ALU; everything else moves one stage on.

  cycle 5
    IF add x4,x1…  ID addi x5,x0…  EX addi x3,x0…  MEM addi x2…  WB addi x1…
    ✓ x1 = 6
    › addi finishes and writes x1 = 6.

  cycle 6
    IF ·  ID add x4, x1, x2  EX addi x5,x0,1  MEM addi x3,x0…  WB addi x2,x0,7
    ✓ x2 = 7
    › addi finishes and writes x2 = 7.

  cycle 7
    IF ·  ID ·  EX add x4, x1, x2  MEM addi x5, x0, 1  WB addi x3, x0, 100
    ✓ x3 = 100
    › addi finishes and writes x3 = 100.

  cycle 8
    IF ·  ID ·  EX ·  MEM add x4, x1, x2  WB addi x5, x0, 1
    ✓ x5 = 1
    › addi finishes and writes x5 = 1.

  cycle 9
    IF ·  ID ·  EX ·  MEM ·  WB add x4, x1, x2
    ✓ x4 = 13
    ✓ add writes x4 = 13, and the program is finished.

  ✓ 9 cycles · 5 instructions · CPI 1.80 · 0 stalls · 0 mispredictions
    Ends with x1 = 6 · x2 = 7 · x3 = 100 · x5 = 1 · x4 = 13
    No stalls: every instruction moved one stage each cycle.

